diff --git a/docs/data-transfers.md b/docs/data-transfers.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..147306e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/data-transfers.md
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# Exporting and importing Fizzy data
+
+Admins can request a full-account export from **Account Settings**. Any member
+can export the cards they can access from their own profile, including their
+own visible drafts. Export preparation runs in a background job and emails a
+signed download link that expires 24 hours after the ZIP is ready. Treat that
+link as a secret. Expired ZIPs are removed by the hourly cleanup task.
+
+Signed-in people can import a full-account ZIP at `/account/imports/new`, even
+without an existing account membership. Imports always create a new account;
+existing accounts are never overwritten. The importer becomes an owner and can
+access every imported board. Other people are matched to local identities by
+email address, or receive a new identity if necessary. They retain their names,
+roles, activation state, and original board access.
+
+Success and failure are reported by email. Invalid versions, card-only exports,
+incomplete archives, corrupt files, and missing or invalid references fail the
+import. The database changes are transactional, and newly uploaded objects are
+removed on failure. The input ZIP is removed after processing.
+
+## Archive format (version 1)
+
+- `manifest.json`: format (`fizzy`), version, export scope, account metadata,
+  export time, record counts by table, and binary file count.
+- `cards/<id>.json`: card attributes, description HTML, comments with body HTML,
+  author names, and attachment metadata pointing to `files/<blob-id>`.
+- `records/<table>/<id>.json`: relational records used for a full-account
+  restoration. This includes boards, columns, users, preferences, cards,
+  comments, tags, assignments, closures, reactions, watches, pins, filters,
+  activity, notifications, entropy settings, rich text, and file metadata.
+- `files/<blob-id>`: original attachment bytes, including card images, rich-text
+  files and pictures, and user avatars. Binary files are stored without ZIP
+  compression; metadata uses deflate. The writer supports ZIP64.
+
+IDs, account slugs, file storage keys, and signed rich-text references are
+regenerated during import. Card numbers and historical timestamps are retained.
+Search indexes and storage accounting are rebuilt. Public board keys and webhook
+signing secrets are regenerated; imported webhooks are disabled until reviewed.
+Credentials, sessions, passkeys, API tokens, device subscriptions, derived image
+variants, and previous export/import files are not included.
+
+## Storage and large uploads
+
+Both local disk and S3 are supported. Local ZIPs are read and written directly
+in storage. S3 ZIP generation and file restoration use multipart streaming, and
+ZIP reading uses buffered range requests. Card comment threads are streamed into
+JSON. Attachments and whole ZIPs are never buffered in memory or copied to worker
+temporary storage. The ZIP directory and individual metadata JSON entries are
+bounded (256 MB and 16 MB respectively) when reading untrusted imports.
+
+The import form uploads directly to storage. S3 uploads use multipart uploads
+with at least 100 MB parts and at most 10,000 parts, supporting archives larger
+than 500 GB (up to S3's 5 TB object limit). Disk uploads use Active Storage's
+standard direct upload. Without JavaScript the form uses a regular multipart
+request; ensure the web server's body limits and temporary disk capacity allow
+it. Background workers and mail delivery must be running.
+
+S3 CORS must allow the application's origin, `PUT` requests, and upload headers,
+and must **expose the `ETag` response header** for multipart uploads. Temporary
+upload tokens belong to the signed-in identity and expire after two days.
+Abandoned uploads, including unfinished S3 multipart uploads, are cleaned up by
+the hourly cleanup task. Failed parts are retried by the browser; failed uploads
+are aborted.
+
+## Regression tests
+
+```sh
+PARALLEL_WORKERS=1 bin/rails test \
+  test/controllers/account/data_transfers_controller_test.rb \
+  test/models/account/data_transfer_test.rb \
+  test/models/account/data_transfer_s3_test.rb \
+  test/models/zip_file_reader_test.rb
+```
+
+A browser smoke test covers the JavaScript/direct-upload form:
+
+```sh
+PARALLEL_WORKERS=1 bin/rails test test/system/data_transfer_test.rb
+```
